\paragraph{$\tau$ as a practical dial.}
$\tau \in [0.5, 0.8]$ all outperform uniform (Table~\ref{tab:tau}), with asymmetric sensitivity: over-cleaning ($\tau > 0.8$) degrades sharply as $\bstar$ inflates, while under-cleaning is mild.
We recommend $\tau = 0.8$ as default; $\tau \in [0.7, 0.8]$ is robust across $\rho \in \{0.4, 0.6\}$ (Appendix~\ref{app:tau_rho}).
